    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d9">

                <pb facs="0095" n="7" sameAs="frus:frus1933v04/pg7"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">710.G 1A/145: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in Colombia</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Dawson</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to
                        the Acting Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Bogotá</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1933-07-13T20:00:00-05:00">July 13, 1933—8
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received 9:05 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>62. Minister for Foreign Affairs is instructing Lozano<anchor n="10"
                        xml:id="d9-f1"/> to approach Department regarding possible presentation to
                    Seventh Pan American Conference of fourth step proposed in President Roosevelt’s
                    disarmament message May 16.<anchor n="11" xml:id="d9-f2"/> His interest is
                    obviously in securing general Pan American commitment not to send armed forces
                    across frontiers. I pointed out that fourth step was suggested as a corollary to
                    fulfillment of three preceding proposals made in message and expressed doubt as
                    to possibility of singling it out for action.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Dawson</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
